A group of Chinese and American scientists have found that urine can react with chemicals in swimming pools that adversely affect the swimmer's respiratory system.
Scientists from the Chinese University of Agriculture and the University of Purdue in the United States mixed pool water with urine and sweat and analyzed it.
Chlorine, a chemical used to kill germs in underwear, reacts with sweat and human urine.
It can adversely affect the lungs and heart through inhalation.
Researchers are urging swimmers to stop this bad habit, as it is an act that is detrimental to human health in general.
