Types of gynecological hair loss and different treatments
In general, about 12 percent of women between the ages of 20 and 24 have hair loss, and this rate increases to 50 percent for women between the ages of 50 and 69.
People often value thick hair as part of their appearance, and women's hair loss is unacceptable, while for men it is considered normal.
Hair loss can be distinguished by the fact that a woman's hair begins to fall out gradually until it becomes very thin, with bald spots appearing on the front, sides, or just above the head, until the scalp is almost visible.
Hair loss can be caused by a variety of factors, such as mental health, stress, malnutrition, scalp infections and hormonal issues, and treatment varies according to the type of hair loss.
Hair loss due to stress does not require any special treatment, instead hair can start to grow gradually in the next few months after we treat those mental problems.
In particular, hair loss can be caused by thyroid disease is necessary to be treated.
Hair loss due to malnutrition can be diagnosed through blood tests to find out which malnourished patients need to be replenished.
Hair loss due to dandruff or fungal infections on the scalp can be treated by using the right shampoo for these problems.
For the treatment of women with hair loss caused by hereditary hormones, it is different from other treatments for hair loss.
Treatment options include applying a scalp lotion containing about 2% minoxidil and twice a day to stimulate the growth of subcutaneous blood vessels and to stimulate the hair follicles to change. A stage where hair can form.
Nowadays, another method that has just appeared on the market is the injection of vitamins necessary to prevent scalp health and stimulate hair cell regrowth.
In addition, lasers can also stimulate hair growth.
However, the use of laser scalp injections is only secondary to the above-mentioned treatments.
In cases where the hair loss is severe and only bare skin remains, only hair transplant surgery can solve this problem.
We can remove the hair follicles at the back of the head and do one planting at a time on the head of the hair loss through the use of anesthetics.
It is a surgery that requires a lot of time and experience from a specialist.
The result is a significant increase in hair volume.
Hair transplants are safe, do not require a break from work or shave, even hairdressers can not know that these women have undergone hair transplants through this surgery.
