How to keep your heart healthy
There is a lot of talk about diet and heart health, and you probably already know how to train well.
You need to know how to control your weight, maintain your obesity level or dissolve your obesity level, and do not eat too much salt.
You should eat soluble fiber from foods such as beans and wheat, you will get a good method of fasting.
All of these are good tips to give you confidence.
A high-fat diet can cause you to gain weight and burn fat, which can raise your cholesterol levels, and eating too much salt can raise your blood pressure. All of these can increase the risk of heart disease.
But for now, we have two more things to watch out for: fatty acids and small molecules, which we call nitric oxide.
You need to make sure that you can maintain a good balance of fatty acids.
When I started counseling patients a few years ago, the dietary record for staying lean was really short and easy to understand and remember: saturated fats are the bad side and insoluble fats. Many other types are good parties.
Simply put, omega-3 fatty acids are good and omega-6 is bad.
Both of these fats are not bad fats, but they are considered essential fatty acids because we need to eat them instead of what our body can not produce.
In small amounts or in the right balance, essential fatty acids perform important functions in the body, such as supporting growth, vision and brain function, and improving blood circulation.
The common problem is that we often consume more omega-6 fatty acids than omega-3s, so the amount of omega-3s is not enough and when we need these two nutrients, if they are not balanced properly, it can affect Our health.
Our modern diet is high in omega-6 fatty acids such as fries, salads, vegetables and desserts.
At the same time, we eat less on foods such as fish, vegetables, walnuts and omega-3 fatty acids.
The good news is that you can change the amount of these fatty acids in your diet.
One healthy practice is to eat a diet made of fish three to four times a week to supply omega-3 fatty acids EPA and DHA for good health.
If you can eat fresh fish is great, but canned fish is easy and has the same benefits, but if you do not like fish, you can eat fish oil that can supply. Give omega-3s to your body as well.
Now we start talking about nitrate and nitric oxide.
Nitric oxide is also an antioxidant that acts to reduce stress in the body and prevent the threat of heart disease.
Nitric oxide is produced from oxygen by our body, along with arginine, an amino acid found in many foods rich in protein, such as whole grains, beans and seafood.
But we can also get from other sources that our bodies can produce nitric oxide from nitrates through the food we eat.
You probably only know that nitrates and nitrates are used as additives for meat stains, such as thighs, to maintain freshness, color, taste, but in fact we can get the least nitrate from the meat we eat.
It can be shown that most of the nitrates we consume come from vegetables and fruits, especially rich in kale, lettuce, celery, cauliflower, grapes, strawberries and tubers.
We already know that vegetables and fruits are good sources of nutrients, they contain antioxidants, fiber, vitamins and minerals, as well as providing vitamins that increase the production of nitric oxide in the body.
