When those foods become carbohydrates, you should try to cut down on starchy foods and replace them with foods rich in soluble fiber found in beans, potatoes, yams and berries. Prunes, kale and carrots can help maintain healthy cholesterol levels.
At the same time, you can get extra nutrients because fruits and vegetables supply enough to keep the heart healthy.
