Is Liposuction With A Tummy Tuck Safe?
Body fat is a concern for everyone.
It causes many problems in life, such as difficulty in dressing, eating and social stigma.
But recently, there is another method that does not require surgery to remove fat cells, as this new method seems to have a lot of controversy regarding the effectiveness as well as the quality of its treatment.
What is the non-surgical method of removing fat cells?
What substances will be injected into the body to get rid of fat cells?
The ingredients in the subcutaneous injection mixture vary greatly depending on the practice of each doctor.
In addition, they can also add vitamins, enzymes and hormones.
But so far it has not been approved for other purposes, such as body fat removal.
However, doctors can use this ingredient for the sole purpose of breaking down fat cells, transporting and preventing the recurrence of fat at the same location.
How is this approach implemented?
The doctor will inject the mixture under the oily layer under the skin without pain, without the need for anesthesia and without having to take a break from work.
These compounds will form a reaction in our body to break down the fat cell envelope quickly.
We see its benefits three weeks after treatment, but it also requires four to five treatments to be effective.
There is a lot of research being done on how fat cells break down and what this is going to be.
There are many claims that the broken cells will enter the bloodstream a little, so it does not cause any problems.
In particular, some opinions that fat cells that break down and will be released out of our body by personal movement.
What is the reality of non-surgical method of breaking down fat cells?
In fact, the method is still in the experimental phase and has not been approved by the US Food and Drug Administration.
The American Medical Association for Plastic Surgery is researching the results and consequences of non-surgical liposuction.
Although six out of seven people who receive this treatment have significantly lower fat levels, they experience side effects such as swelling, redness, pain and itching.
Women who are pregnant, breastfeeding, or patients with diabetes, atherosclerosis, and some other conditions may not be able to receive non-surgical liposuction.
Are you looking for a non-surgical fat cell removal?
Although not officially licensed, a large number of specialists in Europe and the United States have begun to apply these methods.
Non-surgical removal of fat from the abdomen, torso, arms and chin is relatively minor compared to surgery to remove fat cells, which face many problems such as sedation, infection and outcomes. .
