Pregnant women eat peanuts to prevent fetal allergies
According to a new study, children may have a lower risk of food allergies if pregnant women make a habit of eating peanuts or whole grains on a regular basis.
The new study concludes that eating whole grains, especially peanuts, while pregnant may affect the unborn baby.
This grain allergy can cause respiratory problems in children.
In a later study, researchers analyzed data on 8,205 children.
The results showed that children whose mothers ate whole grains during pregnancy had a lower risk of food allergies than children whose mothers did not eat peanuts and whole grains.
Dr. Lindsay Fraser, of Boston, USA, said:
How much protein do you need?
Do you know how much protein our body needs to eat?
Today I will show you how to calculate the amount of protein you need and share a list of important foods along with protein levels.
The amount of protein your body needs depends on many factors, such as weight and muscle size, whether in a woman or a man.
Just by reading documents online, you can never know exactly how much protein your body actually needs.
The Food Council guidelines of most medical institutes state that women generally need an average of 46 grams of protein per day, compared to men 56 grams per day.
You need to know that this figure is set to suit the basic needs of most people only.
Does this formula work for everyone?
The calorie requirement for each person is different and so is the protein requirement.
Everyone is different in size, shape and composition, so everyone needs a different amount of protein.
For example, a 100-kilogram construction worker who exercises daily and a 68-kilogram bank employee sitting in one place would both need the same amount of protein.
Another guideline from the Institute of Medicine suggests that 10 to 35 percent of our total daily calories should come from a protein diet.
This guide links protein diets to calorie requirements.
But with this figure, can you calculate the estimated amount of calories and protein for your body?
Since protein is important for maintaining muscle and body, the amount of protein you need also depends on your size.
You can make measurements through the scales.
Then you can determine the amount of protein your body needs, with one kilogram of body weight you need 1 to 2 grams of protein.
Of course, not everyone knows how to analyze their body composition.
But if you do not know how to calculate, you can also estimate your body weight.
This method is not perfect, but at least it allows you to find the right amount of protein for your own body size.
The way to calculate the amount of protein you need is to multiply your weight in kilograms by 1.5.
The result you get is equal to the number of grams of protein your body needs to consume daily.
If a woman weighs 64 kilograms, she should eat 100 grams of protein a day.
For a man who weighs 110 kilograms, he should eat at least 150 grams of protein a day.
The amount of protein stored in your daily diet After finding out how much protein your body needs, you may now want to know how much protein you are consuming per day.
I think we can easily estimate that one meal contains 25 grams of protein and 10 grams for a snack.
The food we eat at one time usually contains about 25 grams of protein.
At each meal, our body can get 10 grams of protein.
For a lady who needs 100 grams of protein a day, she can get 25 grams of protein by eating one meal out of three meals and 20 grams from two meals.
For a healthy man who needs 150 grams of protein, he can eat the same food by eating twice the amount to get the right level of protein for his body weight.
