Korean smile lip surgery
The size, shape and thickness of a woman's lips are also a factor that can make us predict the characteristics of a woman.
On the same painting, but in the case of lips with both edges falling off, it clearly shows the distress, especially in the same photo, if the edges of both lips of a woman are closer, it shows Happiness instead.
That's why in South Korea, there is a tendency for lip surgery to make the shape more beautiful, with the edges closer to create a smile.
Before exploring lip correction methods, we should first understand the anatomical characteristics of this limb.
Everyone's lips are composed of many types of muscles that play a role in opening and closing and smiling.
The lips have three groups of muscles: the group that plays the role of pulling the edges of our lips up, the group that pulls to the side, and the group that pulls down.
So, in principle, to get a lip with both edges up, it is necessary to increase the strength of the upper muscles and reduce the muscles that play a role in pulling down the edge of the lips.
These surgeries require us to remove a small portion of the skin of the upper lip, and then we perform a reduction in the force of the lower extremity contractions and an increase in the upper extremity contractions.
Smiley Liposuction is a procedure that is not as complicated as other facial surgeries.
We can perform these surgeries in a sterile operating room medically, using the right equipment and performing anesthesia.
But before the surgery, doctors need to study the client to find out if it is a psychological factor or other necessity for this smile-making surgery.
Surgery can be simple and takes about 40 minutes to an hour, depending on the doctor's experience.
After the operation, the client will have sutures on the upper edge of both lips.
These sutures can be removed within a week after surgery.
We also need to consider the consequences of it, which can lead to uneven lip edges or scarring at the surgical site, especially for fair-skinned women.
