Long-distance plane riders may have blood clots
Long-distance travel by plane or car can put people at higher risk for blood clots, especially in the calves and thighs.
Sitting for long periods of time while traveling by plane or car can cause blood clots and blood clots.
The blood flowed to parts of the human body through veins.
