If possible, most couples would rather have a son or a daughter than give birth to all-male or all-female children.
Separately, some parents also have the view of wanting the eldest son or eldest daughter for various reasons.
Therefore, determining the sex of the baby is a popular topic for couples who want to start a family.
Although science has not yet been able to determine the sex of a baby 100 percent, fertility experts have made a number of recommendations to increase the chances of having the desired baby boy or girl.
Understand the scientific process of fertilization The sex of the baby is determined at the time of conception.
The sex of a child, male or female, depends on the chromosome when the two sperm, the ovum and the spermatozoon, meet.
X-XX chromosomes give birth to daughters, while XY-X chromosomes give birth to sons.
Beliefs about the sex of the baby There are many documents that describe the dreams of men and women in determining the sex of their baby from before the operation of conception to conception.
Some say that if you want a daughter, you have to have sex with your partner before ovulation and eat salt to have a son.
Some people believe that eating red meat will help get a daughter.
In the early stages of pregnancy, some people believe that women who want to eat seafood and desserts are more likely to have a son, while those who eat red meat and pickles are more likely to have a daughter.
Regarding the shape of the abdomen, some people believe that a flat abdomen is definitely a daughter's abdomen, while a long, sharp abdomen is more likely to be a son's abdomen.
Some people also believe that the sex of the child is related to the weather, the zodiac sign of the month, birth, season and so on.
EFFECTS OF Diet According to French doctor Fran ស្វois Papa, dietary restrictions for mothers in the months leading up to pregnancy have a direct effect on the cervix, enabling spermatozoa to pass through it.
A diet that reduces salt and is rich in calcium and magnesium increases the acidity in the cervical mucus, which is conducive to spermatogenesis.
To be effective, you must eat this diet every day without interruption for 4 months before pregnancy.
In addition, women should also be aware that the use of certain medications also interferes with the benefits of eating this diet.
The timing of sexual intercourse determines the sex of the baby, having sex before ovulation can be up to 5 days before having a chance to have a baby girl.
Having sex before or after ovulation for up to 2 days will increase the chances of having a baby boy.
Mucus in the cervix stimulates sperm to pass into the uterus when the ovum falls.
Before ovulation, spermatozoa are difficult to pass through.
Sperm can pass through at a slower rate, so a passable spermatozoon is a daughter with an X chromosome, a female spermatozoon because it has a longer lifespan than a Y chromosome.
During and after ovulation, the sperm with the Y chromosome is the fastest, thus giving birth to a son.
For women with regular periods, the cycle of ovulation is 14 days from the day of menopause.
Sexual practices Some people think that they can increase their chances of having a son or daughter of their choice.
Time and frequency of intercourse.
There is little scientific evidence to support such an idea, but you can also try it if you wish to have a son or a daughter.
For girls, have sex a little more often, as this can reduce the amount of sperm containing the Y chromosome in semen.
For boys, you should have sex a little less because it can increase the amount of sperm that contain the Y chromosome in semen.
