Botak treats facial wrinkles
What is Botak and how does it work?
Botox is a protein produced by a virus that has been modified to be used to treat a number of ailments related to the contraction of facial or neck muscles.
What beauty problems can Bothok treat?
Of course, wrinkles on the face, forehead, tail, eyes, neck and eyebrows often occur as we age.
Botox injections on a particular site can block the control of nerves that cause muscle spasms.
Botox is used as a first-line treatment for wrinkles caused by over-acting on the face, but it is not used in the treatment of any wrinkles that occur on the face on a regular basis.
It is also used to reduce the appearance of fine lines and wrinkles on the lips.
In addition, it can help our scars from wrinkles, especially on the muscles.
It will last about 3 to 4 times after treatment.
The treated muscles will remain normal, allowing us to laugh, smile or frown without problems.
The upper part of the face, especially around the forehead, is an area where we can get the best results, as it can reduce the wrinkles on the corners of the eyes, around the eyes or between the eyebrows.
Doctors can also correct eyebrow problems, which usually decline with age, can help balance for clients who have facial nerve problems due to trauma during surgery.
It is a short and easy method and we can return to work immediately after treatment.
When should we receive Botox injections?
We should start treatment when we feel wrinkles on the face and forehead, then we need to take care not to wrinkle again.
The use of Botox requires regularity every six months.
What other problems can Botox use?
Botox has recently been approved for use in the UK to treat headaches, and it is also widely used to treat excessive sweating on the armpits and palms, which can lead to poor communication. Days.
What are the possible consequences of using Botox?
Although it is a popular beauty treatment, it can also cause side effects such as headaches, dizziness and nausea.
At the same time, other complications can also be caused by improper treatment or lack of technique by doctors.
The extent of these complications depends on many factors, such as the location of the injection and the experience of the doctor performing the procedure.
One of the most common side effects is sagging of the upper eyelids or dryness of the eyes caused by the use of bots around the eyes to reduce the appearance of fine lines and wrinkles.
Some complications can also be caused by the use of poor quality botox, making it easier to flow to other places after the botox injection operation.
Other side effects of using botox in the neck area include difficulty swallowing or breathing.
However, these side effects can be alleviated after Botox is out of action within a month after use.
Although we can not completely avoid the complications, we can reduce the negative problems by using good quality boots and following the proper techniques from an experienced doctor.
